    "%lldth" : {

    },
    "**5T** is the classic game: lines may share an end dot. **5D** is stricter — lines along the same direction may not touch at all. **4T** and **4D** use lines of four from a smaller start, and are short enough to solve. **5T+** loosens up: the dot and the line come apart, so five dots already in a row do count." : {

